  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "lpLAG/B65Pr2ujftcK9Lr6F524M=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:08.105Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "TPXimpact is a listed UK public-sector pure play at GBP 78.1m, and the research notes it is recovering. The reason it appears next to Made Tech is that both draw the same regulatory tailwind: UK public sector operates under an open-source-by-default mandate, so a supplier's posture is set by the buyer rather than chosen by the supplier.\n\nBeing a pure play sharpens that. A mixed consultancy can treat default-open government work as one practice among several, with its own carve-outs; a firm whose whole revenue base is public sector has no non-mandated business to fall back on, so every engagement carries the same disclosure expectations.\n\nThe recovery note is the risk to weigh against it \u2014 a listed firm working through a downturn is likely to be selective about unfunded pilots. Nothing in the record establishes its stack or its own contribution history; only the regime and the shape of the business are on file. Priority 2.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- TPXimpact (UK \u00b7 GBP 78.1m)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Public-sector pure play, listed, recovering. Same regulatory tailwind as Made Tech.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:08.105368Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:08.105372Z"
    }
  },
